elfth; her ruling was "not on my plank". **Her finding** ("There's a place in you I can't read because it isn't *flow* …") is known to Cael and Lira. **Cael's own — the twelfth turned inward unbidden under her hands: *still*, then *set* — is told to NO ONE**, and the next word was not let come; Lira knows only that something unasked came and is waiting; the log holds four reasons and the ruling *hold*. Oryn has not heard the leaf ("Tell me on the road, if there's road. Not at my table."). Cleon's warning has "begun to lean". She walks east in the middle of the file with the mule, on nobody's count: three holds owed on her round; "I'm a stop on my own route." (8) **Bodies at dawn on the 299th:** Brom's left shoulder mended, the right re-tied, both arms to shoulder height; Lira's arm released ("It's an arm."); Karis's stitches out, linen on, "Write. Don't lean."; Teague's right wrist in linen under the leather. (9) **Watchers:** a horseman a mile behind on the 296th and a riderless horse in the western alders on the 297th; nothing seen east of the river; no face, name or base. (10) **Seln's case is "shut"** — never write "unopened" or "locked … unopened" (this packet's cutaway note says so and is overridden here); on his chest; contents unnamed; no count of years printed.
