   347	The tall man turned his spear about, so that its head lay toward the west; the broad man got his stick under him, and the old woman took up her board. They did not go anywhere; the light was nearly gone, and there were seven miles of rock between that place and a gap. But they had turned. Their packs went round to the western side of the fire, and they sat down with their backs to the floor, three people and a healer of no Path, who had come the length of a country on another crew's line and had left one of their own at a gap in it.
   348	
