   251	He had been set there as a mark. It was a kind of posting, and it was the first that he had held since he left a seal in a tray; and he found that he had no wish to end it merely because the thing that it served was done. A round had been shut upon the foot of his stick, six hours since, by a girl walking heel to toe. He had felt the slip of ash touch the wood. Not many acts of his own life had been of such plain use to anybody.
