   182	
   183	Across the gravel a stick had been laid down. The old man sat with his leg out along a blanket, and the lean old woman, going by with her kettle, stopped and looked at two laths and a healer's linen as a joiner looks at another shop's door. She said nothing to him, and went on; and he inclined his head to her back, gravely, by about the width of a finger, as one office acknowledges a paper from another.
   184	
