   239	"I shut that shoulder on the two hundred and ninety-eighth. A mend that deep wants a week of somebody's eye, and I've said in a yard what I think of a healer who spends herself on a thing and walks off while it's deciding. That's the three hundred and fifth." Her hand had come up, and a thumb went down. "There's a knee behind it that's on my linen and twenty-one days old. And there's an edge at the end of that brass that's twice any I've stood at, with ten of you going at it. I said in a loft where somebody ought to be."
