editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-19.md:95:"No. So I don't know what a station does with it. That's the whole of my reason, and it's no better than that. I've no finding. I've a thing that I can't read, and a thing that reads, and I'd not walk any patient of mine past the one with the other in him until I knew." Her voice had not risen. "You go inside, you don't go near the station. Not the steps, not the square. You promise me in that log of yours, because I've seen what the log does to you."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-19.md:109:*The fork. Oryn north; five holds; routing, not the other verb. Her term, given at the fire, taken in the log because that's the form she'll take it in: inside Treswick I do not go near the station. Not the steps. Not the square. Written here so she can read it, and so I can.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-19.md:231:"Not the steps," she said. "Not the square."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-42.md:109:It came to him quite plainly, between one stride and the next. A healer had made him write a thing in a book at a fork-stone: that inside Treswick he did not go near the station. He had kept it for thirteen days, to the letter, down a lane with four white alleys in it, and through a night when a thread of light on a loft's boards had not been steady. And the gate was behind him. The river was the Line, and he was over the river. The promise had been for inside, and he was out.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-42.md:227:He went over that as he walked, since the road asked for nothing but his feet. There had been a boy on this moor fourteen days ago with a date in him that he had not written down, and a page that he had not touched, and a promise in a book. That boy had been afraid of a gate. He had thought that the worst thing a town could do was to write his name.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-37.md:269:*The promise stands. Not the steps. Not the square.*

