editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-007/source-tracking.stdout.log:899:    73	Oryn looked at Brom, once, and said nothing, and rebound the hand with her own linen, tighter and flatter, and said to Karis, "It'll close. It'll leave a line. Don't write with it for a week — the other hand. You've got one." And Karis, who had been writing with it for eight days and would not stop for a week, said "Noted," which from Karis was not agreement, and Oryn heard that it was not and let it go, because a healer picks the orders she enforces.
