editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-40.md:49:"I can't tell you what it means," he said. "She'll not, and she's the one who can read it, so I'll not. I can tell you what it cost."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-40.md:57:"He was as frightened as that. You can read it off the bill; it's the only part of him that's left." Brom looked into the fire. "I'm not saying that he'd cause. A price isn't a verdict. I've known a man pay a great deal for a bad horse, and swear by it after, because of what he'd paid."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-30.md:191:"The third is twelve again. And the last is seven: a ring, and two." Her voice had gone thin and quick. "Those are figures. I can read his figures. I have not been able to read one mark of this in a year, and I can read how many."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-38.md:97:"I can read it."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-38.md:189:"I can read this at sight," she said. "It is the old town's hand. It is the hand of the tally-books, or its father's." Her pencil went down the leaf without touching. "It is a chronicle. It has the floods in it, and a murrain among the cattle, and who was reeve. Somebody of this town kept a year-book, and somebody else laid it away with that."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-41.md:57:"I can spell it," she said. "I can very nearly say it aloud, as a child says a word in a tongue that it has not been taught. It is a noun, and then a number, and the number I can read." Her pencil tapped. "The noun stands on the face as well. It is the first of the four things that he says were made."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-41.md:135:"The first run I can read," said Karis. She was writing with the bound hand, very small, and her lips were white. "It is the people at a kindling, as the face has them. The second run is six signs, and it is in the thin; and of the six I am certain of three."
19:### Entry (Book 7 close; source Ch1 opens on the hundred and thirty-first day past the Line)
21:- **When/where:** Lowmarch, the hundred and thirty-first morning, after the Book 7 hearth scene at the lower inn. The first snow fell on day 129; the last ferry crossed and its lines were taken in on day 130; Oryn's letter arrived through a hand's depth of snow on day 131. Book 8 continues later that morning. The Book 8 count remains day 131 to day 308. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4]
22:- **Cael:** nineteen. **There is no birthday in this book.** His own Arbiter woke at Kindling, its plate lit eleven seconds late, the failed-safe word replaced the old name, and it went dark; he has no Path. He has **ten confirmed fragments**: Wind (Lira), Pressure (`the Bronze from Ardenmere` in spoken inventories), Iron (Brom), Compression (Reydan), Ember (Karis), Shadow (Seln; sealed; used exactly twice, at Ring and Stair), Storm (Daeva), Anchor (unnamed; used once each way), Blade (Ephram), and Tide (Oryn; partial; Iron; self and contact; clinical; *ask first, every time*). Deployment since the Line: **twenty-seven**. **The still place** is not a fragment and is not counted: read three times, told to Oryn and then described to the other four, untouched since Oryn ordered him to write it down and stop touching it. His ribs have been quiet since the morning of day 129. The living purse holds 96 marks. Open accounts are listed below; `nothing owed` is false. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4]
39:- **Vastin** is on the stick until the thirtieth day of Oryn's treatment month [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] ("Thirty's the month"). He walks with the five **unadmitted**. He has not asked to join and nobody has asked him.
40:- **Oryn** turns north on her mule at dawn ("The day I have to." / "After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]). She has **not heard the leaf**. She still owes three holds.
44:- **Body ledger at close:** Brom's forearm is bound (bolt, pass) and he has a week of colours. Karis's left hand is bound and will scar ("It'll leave a line"). The broad man's leg is knit and his shoulder bound. Teague's arm faces a splint warning. Vastin is on day 29 of 30. Cael's ribs "will carry. They'll hurt."
54:2. **KEEP — Pike's cold-term board and the fence (140th).** [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] Two days out to the axe-head hold. Forty-one posts. Seln finds two of Teague's posts a hand off true and tells only Brom. Forty is paid at the gate: 116. PAID becomes the tenth line.
58:6. **KEEP — Thornwater (265th–266th).** The ford in thaw. Oryn's yard. Lira's arm is released ("Five months and twenty days." [OWNER-pending #56] / "That's a season. Take it off."). Lira asks, for the first time since Norhold: "Will you mend it." / "Lie still". The ankle is mended. "Thank you." / "Route's whole. The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks." The map on Thornwater's table: "That's a line." Cael tells her about the cord: "I don't know what that is. Neither do you. Write that down too." Oryn comes down because Lowmarch and Millrace are her first stops after the thaw [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6]. Nobody asked her.
61:9. **KEEP — The long table (277th midday).** The Seln–Vastin doorway exchange, their first words ever. The short thing: resigned or walked. Brom: "Three hundred miles is a demonstration." The layer: Karis supplies its existence; Vastin's new fact is "Cannot. There is no key." The name is a citation to a designer, and the trail dead-ends at Treswick. Vastin has nothing to do afterwards. "Why us." Oryn on the knee: "Then I still haven't asked." "What follows you": nothing that can cross the Line. Cael remembers the Book 6 sentence and says only: "Ask him the thing you want to ask him." Karis asks; Vastin's close (§10). The ferry goes west.
65:13. **KEEP — The spring (280th).** Three readers: Karis for pattern, Seln for omission, Vastin for procedure. The office's instruments. **"Behaves as device. Cannot be."** Karis stops her lamps sentence with the ruler rule. **The grade:** the same stroke and bar on all four sites, the fourth's twice the size. "Two copies of one ignorance." Vastin's three reflexes: directive, classification, "This has to go up". The second row counts a sheet short in Cael's hands. Seln sets the technician's sheet before Cael without a word. Cael does the sum (the date matches his Kindling day; "six years" is the office's survey-record rounding; no numeric span since Kindling is computed [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 7]), does **not** write it down, and puts the sheet back. "You keep drafting orders." / "Habit." / "Out here the habit's the tell. Draft nothing. Just look." Cleon is named for the first time.
67:15. **KEEP — The last day of the road (281st).** Lira makes the same discipline of the crown, unasked. The reading inward, a fourth and fifth time: "a cord on a stone"; the instrument is wrong for a stillness. Vastin sits; "You were the instrument. I was the error." Vastin's confession, narrowed (ruling 18): "I declined to read you a second time. You know that. What you do not know is why." Cael gives him the instrument's nothing. It is not friendship; it is ground. The log (§10).
75:23. **KEEP — The reader (291st).** By the carts' street in daylight. Cleon's inside: "An instruction leans … This is a stair." Karis: "The strata lean too." **Acquisition at "there".** Cael tells Lira first ("Twelfth. His. Lean."), then Cleon at the bell. "You did what." "That's not supposed to be possible. That's —" / "No. I'll not say that one." The cup of water; **the warning**. "He went back to the carving." Vastin and Cael take the case up together. The notice on the stair. The eyes are paid on the last flight. "Cael did not tell anyone. He remembered."
77:25. **KEEP — The leaf (293rd morning).** It is read aloud **once** by Karis (§9). The chronicle leaf is **marked**. Vastin reaches ("the mark that is given at the kindling —") and Karis answers: two pages. The copy with the gap drawn. "Older. Made. Us."
81:29. **KEEP — Force seen (298th morning).** The meadow cart: the frame lined up heel to palm, a body's length; the wrist clicks; the young one's cloth. "Don't put it in front of anything that needs doing twice."
82:30. **KEEP — The grade cracked (298th morning).** Three marks. Cleon's list puts the mark at the kindling and the mark on a sheet in one line: "A mark is a grade." Ages by first sheet: 61, 94, 138, 206. The third-tier point lies past the fourth, on the line. **Oldest-last.** "It's observation." **Vastin's first "Noted."** Teague: "Oldest last." / "Then that's where we're going." The log (§10).
83:31. **KEEP — Millrace (298th evening–299th dawn).** "Eleven off the ridge." / "I know." The two healers look at each other and then at Brom's shoulder. Vastin is ordered to stand ("Nineteen days." / "Then it's eleven more.") and takes the order without walking it back. Oryn's terms restated. "Sixth chair." / "On my terms. Which are the only kind." **She asks each patient first ("May I?").** The readings: shoulder, arm ("Once is once more than I priced"), Karis's hand ("Who sewed this."), the knee ("It held in a cut"; "Noted" / "That's new." / "It's a useful word." / "It's his."). **The deep reading**, with consent. **Rune turns inward unbidden: *still*, then *set*.** Withheld. Oryn's finding (§10). The leaf is offered: "Tell me on the road, if there's road. Not at my table." Twelve and a mule at dawn.
122:4. **The Deepstacks decipherment** (≈8,000). The chamber days 285–292 are put on the page, including the undramatized 288th–289th. Cleon's method (bones before words), the board's numerals, Karis's letters coming one at a time from the three floors, and the lamp's discipline. Karis refuses to guess. **The leaf must not become readable on the page before the seventh day** (§13).
131:- **Treswick's days** (≈8,000). The outer district as a mechanism: brokers' tally boards, the smith's two forges, the ring road at night. The undramatized chamber days.
132:- **The 294th: the list of parts** (≈2,000). Copying all day, Cleon's finger on the last line, and his correction "Your hand's better than mine on the fourth line".
146:| **Oryn** | The route; to be nobody's recruit | Releases the arm only when Lira lifts the sling herself. Comes to Lowmarch unasked. Sets the station term in the log. Routes north. Rejoins as a stop. Asks every time. Walks on east at the cairn. Will not hear the leaf at her table. Turns north "the day I have to". | 11 |
173:| 5 | No Authority | 27–33 | 35,000 | S10, S11, S12 | The archive's first days; Vastin unlearning his name; Cleon's bones; Brom offered the life; the alley and the eleventh. |
195:| **Seln** | ≈7,500 (4) | M3: the spring, doing the sum and setting the sheet. M5: the night walk on the roof with the cache. M8: the crest at night or the perimeter before the Span. M9: the ridge with Lira to recover the mule. | The sum (the date ≈ Cael's Kindling day), unspoken; the office's habits; the faction's craft; the cache's existence and weight. | **The cache's contents** (it stays unopened). Any decision about the cache. Any theory of what the deep layer is. The Rune finding. Teaching anyone before Vastin at the spring. |
