    21	She had not raised her voice; she had said it as she would have read a figure off a slip, and she had said it to the fire.
    22	
    23	Nobody answered, and when she spoke again it was of another thing.
    24	
    25	"There's a hole in it. She's ruled a box, with nothing inside."
    26	
    27	"There is a hole in the skin," said Karis, without opening her eyes. "I have drawn it as it is."
    28	
    29	"There's a stroke in the hole."
    30	
    31	"Yes."
