    52	
    53	"I'll not say it over; she's asked. I'll only say how big it is. Whatever was built, by that page, was built over the whole of the country, and down to every child in it. That's not a fence round a field. I saw what my father paid to keep foxes off forty hens, and he grudged every nail." He rubbed his jaw with the back of his wrist, since he could not lift the hand. "This is every stone turned over, and every one of us weighed, to keep out one sort of person. Nobody spends so on a thing that he thinks is small."
    54	
    55	"He was frightened," said Lira.
