    71	She had not opened her eyes; she sat with her bound hand on her notebook, and her head had begun to go forward; but the voice was her own.
    72	
    73	"There is what that leaf says. And there is everything else that any of us knows, or thinks that he knows, about floors, or anything." She drew a breath that was half a yawn, and was too tired to be ashamed of it. "I have filled the one. The other is clean. Nobody is to write upon it while I am asleep."
    74	
    75	"I only said *so*."
    76	
