269:He had stepped across it at dusk. It had been one stride, upon a stick, with a leg that a healer had bound; and the thing that had stood beside his face since he was fourteen had gone out.
CHAPTER-60
17:He had added three words to an entry that had stood unaltered since a session with a healer, on the far side of a cold term. They were not a finding. Karis would have told him so, and she would have been right, since no ruler had been laid on anything. They were only what he had said aloud on a floor, to nobody, with his palm on his own chest. He had put them down because he would not keep a book that left out the one thing which he had walked a year to say.
151:[[TIER-B: Teague's departure — "The thaw's past," / "Noted," / "After the next thaw." … "Whatever's on the next line. My crew comes." — Tier A 22 heads the unit "Teague:" but does not say which of the first two lines is his and which the answer, and it elides between "After the next thaw." and "Whatever's on the next line." Staged here: dawn of the 308th at the western side of the fire, Teague a stride from Cael with the letter already in his coat, his three standing behind him; the term that he set at Lowmarch ("After the thaw. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes.") has been kept, and this is its successor. Nothing of mine stands between his last speech above and this unit; the paragraph below has him go — coordinator to supply protected text]]
179:She went along them, before she would get up, as she had gone along six people at a fork-stone. She looked under the linen on Brom's forearm, having asked, and told him that he was to keep it out of the wet and that the colours on his chest were coming on nicely. She took Karis's left hand, by her leave, and turned it to the light. She told Lira nothing whatever, since there was nothing that wanted telling, and Lira said that she had noticed.
203:[[TIER-B: Oryn's departure — "The day I have to." / "Noted," / "Everybody says that." … "They'll carry. They'll hurt," … "After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say." — Tier A 22 heads the unit "Oryn:" and elides twice; the "Noted," between her first and third lines is not pinned. Staged here: dawn of the 308th at the rim, the mule unloaded, three boxes on the rock at Cael's feet; her first line answers his question above about the leaf (she has still not heard it); "Noted," reads as his; "They'll carry. They'll hurt," is said of his ribs with her eyes on the box that he must take up; the last line is her term, as in her letter. If "The day I have to." answers something else, my question above wants turning. The paragraph below has her go — coordinator to supply protected text]]
255:He slung it above his sound leg, and came across the rock, at his own beat, and stopped a stride behind a big man with a box, where he had stood since a ford. He looked at nobody. He had asked nothing of any of them, that morning or on any other, and nobody had asked a thing of him.

