+### 5.3 §9 and §11, line by line
+
+- `four hundred years` appears in this movement only in the protected closing (`chapter-60.md:277`), as required by `BOOK_MAP.md:334`. `the Architect` does not appear. The leaf is not quoted and is never joined to the lamps finding (`chapter-57.md:91`; `chapter-59.md:249–343`; `BOOK_MAP.md:338`).
+- No `terminal`, `circuit` or `infrastructure` appears. The Arbiter never speaks; it is only checked dark (`chapter-57.md:173–177,255`; `BOOK_MAP.md:421`). The deep-layer date is neither printed nor calculated (`chapter-54.md:3–361`; `chapter-60.md:3–277`; `BOOK_MAP.md:339`).
+- Vastin's apparatus sentence stays stopped (`chapter-59.md:323`); his cutaway contains no leaf, lamps join, date arithmetic or Book 9 request (`chapter-59.md:249–343`). Oryn has not heard the leaf (`chapter-57.md:91`; `chapter-60.md:197–203`). There is no cutaway at the court itself; Cael is alone there (`chapter-59.md:3–185`).
+- The third sentence is neither stated nor paraphrased outside the protected closing. `He fit`, `It was not an accident`, `Here the foot arrived`, `He did not know what it was instead`, and “a step beyond ... left lying” are all expressly permitted plan beats, not completion of the sentence (`chapter-59.md:137–185`; `EVENT-LIST.md:52`). `he was the pattern` appears only inside the exact protected closing (`chapter-60.md:277`).
+- The site has no agency. The affirmative attention metaphors outside protected text all belong to fragments/tools whose fixed behavior is to listen/read: Force `found` the ridge and `did not ask` (`chapter-54.md:251–253`); Force had `not looked` at the frame and may have `found` a line, `wanted` a word and `waited` (`chapter-55.md:167,233,239`); Rune `looked`, is given something to look at, `gave` a shape and is called a tool that could look (`chapter-57.md:193,199,215,233`); the folded Rune thing turns “as a head ... to the only voice” (`chapter-58.md:49`); Force is `listening` and Rune is deliberately allowed to `look` and `gave` a shape (`chapter-59.md:27,55,71,127`). These are established functional metaphors for the fragments (`EVENT-LIST.md:7,20,35,52`), not attention assigned to the court or a machine. The explicit negatives remain: cord/light/made things do not know (`chapter-57.md:163`) and the floor does not know (`chapter-59.md:165`). The only sentence that crosses into intentional instrument agency is `a brass rule lied` at `chapter-59.md:147`; fix 10 removes it together with adjacent plate/registry personification.
