+## 7. Names
+
+**PASS.** No unapproved proper name is minted. Proper names used in this movement—Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln, Vastin, Oryn, Teague, Cleon, Hesk, Pike, Ostrand, Ternhall, Denvash, Lowmarch, the Fallow, the Stair and the Span—are all already in the edition plan or closed text (`BOOK_MAP.md:480–484`; `chapter-54.md:3–361`; `chapter-60.md:3–277`). Pike, Hesk and Lowmarch are referenced but do not appear physically (`chapter-60.md:71,79,137–143`), consistent with `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:132`.
+
+The deliberately unnamed roles are: the young one/Teague's boy; the tall man/spear-carrier; the broad man/bow; the lean old woman/healer of no Path; nine hooded pass opponents (three bowmen, one maul-man, five others); the woman near her time at Oryn's middle hold; and the old man whose chest Oryn hears at the last hold (`chapter-54.md:19–35,189–205`; `chapter-55.md:97–147,273–289`; `chapter-57.md:43,75–93`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:118`). The broad man saying the young one's name without rendering its sound follows #54 and does not mint it on the page (`chapter-55.md:143–147`).
+
+## 8. Book exit state for the Book 9 planner
+
+There is no Movement 10 packet. This is the complete state at the last line.
+
+### People, routes and counts
+
+- **Date:** dawn of the 308th past the Line (`chapter-60.md:103–277`; `BOOK_MAP.md:247`).
+- **West, six and no mule:** Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln and Vastin (`chapter-60.md:249–273`; `BOOK_MAP.md:43`). Vastin is physically with them but unadmitted: no request, invitation or vote has occurred (`chapter-59.md:309–323`; `chapter-60.md:255–265`; `BOOK_MAP.md:39,424`).
+- **North:** Oryn rides the brown mule toward the two-days-up salt road and three owed holds. She is eight days past the cairn and still owes three holds (`chapter-60.md:171–223`; `chapter-49.md:79`; `BOOK_MAP.md:40`).
+- **West separately:** Teague, the tall man, the broad man and the lean old woman go toward the pass/cairn and Lowmarch. Teague carries Cael's letter for Hesk's bag and is one short without saying the number (`chapter-60.md:131–165`; `BOOK_MAP.md:41`).
+- **Dead:** the unnamed young one is under a cairn at the pass's east mouth. The broad man said the name once; Cael does not write it (`chapter-55.md:113–147`; `chapter-56.md:3–59`; `chapter-57.md:249`).
+- **Opposition:** nine faceless opponents withdrew east along the ridge; none was taken or struck in retreat. Their base and names remain unknown (`chapter-55.md:269–299`; `chapter-56.md:71–83`; `BOOK_MAP.md:42`).
+
+### Cael and the instruments
+
+- Nineteen; no birthday placed. Thirteen fragments: Wind, Pressure, Iron, Compression, Ember, Shadow, Storm, Anchor, Blade, Tide, Iron Wall, Rune, Force. Deployment since the Line **35** (`chapter-60.md:13,23,37,71`; `BOOK_MAP.md:34`).
+- Force used once, on the second stack's brace, along the shelf, at nobody; cost returned to the old ribs. Iron Wall remains unused by him. Rune was deliberately turned inward once as an uncounted self-reading and deliberately turned on the court floor once as deployment 35 (`chapter-55.md:199–253`; `chapter-57.md:179–241,259`; `chapter-59.md:49–77`; `chapter-60.md:23`).
+- Still place: Tide says nothing/flow goes around it; Rune says *Still / Set / Bones*, a floor with nothing built on it, an instruction with no language, the same kind of thing to that instrument as the sites to Cleon's. At the centre there was no edge or seam. Cael alone knows the inward finding, the identical floor reading and the centre's absence of an edge (`chapter-57.md:179–241`; `chapter-59.md:49–185`; `BOOK_MAP.md:34,431`).
+- Arbiter dark and unchanged. Cord a stride short in forty-two; Ternhall a hair and a half short; Hesk's two hairs long in Cael's hand, true in others'. Trend up, cause unsourced, no line drawn (`chapter-57.md:103–177,255`; `BOOK_MAP.md:34`).
+- Body: two ribs cracked along the old line, third sore; they carry and hurt. Eyes recovered from the floor reading (`chapter-56.md:295–305`; `chapter-59.md:49–77,189–213`; protected departure to restore at `chapter-60.md:203`).
+
+### Other bodies
+
+- Brom: bolt through left forearm, bound; colours across chest/old bruises for about a week; both shoulders otherwise usable. He carries the heaviest box and Oryn's bowl obligation (`chapter-55.md:5–33`; `chapter-60.md:179,217–243`).
+- Karis: left palm bound and usable; after fix 16 the exit records that it will leave a line. She carries the flat, hide and notebook (`chapter-60.md:179,247`; `BOOK_MAP.md:44`).
+- Vastin: right knee day 29 of 30, sound and a day from done; linen/laths and stick remain for that day. He carries the tarred case (`chapter-60.md:9,183–191,249–255`).
+- Teague: right arm on slat, hand not shutting, third-use splint warning standing; takes letter left-handed (`chapter-60.md:131–149`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:883`).
+- Broad man: right shin knit/boarded; right shoulder shut and bound across the chest; pine stick; no new injury after the pass (`chapter-55.md:323–327`; `chapter-60.md:121–129,165`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:149`).
+- Lira: arm whole; no new injury. Oryn: physically uninjured, carrying the first death under her hands. Seln: physically uninjured, case shut on chest. Tall man and lean old woman: uninjured (`chapter-57.md:3–99`; `chapter-60.md:103–129,165–223`).
+
+### Money, loads, pages and debts
+
+- Purse 123; nothing owed in money and nothing spent in this movement (`chapter-60.md:9,25`; `EVENT-LIST.md:60`). Reserve remains sealed in the third/lightest box, now on Cael; Brom has the heaviest, Lira the second (`chapter-60.md:227–247`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:887`).
+- Karis: sixty-one sheets (original fifty-two plus the nine pier sheets), calfskin with five rings/ending line, Ternhall brass, notebook containing the torn lamps leaf and separate no-second-page entry, and Cleon's materials as previously carried (`chapter-60.md:83–87,247`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:887,900`).
+- Cael: Hesk's book, Hesk's dividers, folded fair copy of the chamber leaf, log including the unread inward-reading entry, and letter no longer in hand (`chapter-57.md:245–297`; `chapter-60.md:71,135–139`).
+- Vastin: tarred case with twenty-stride cord, mallet and never-driven stake thirty-two (`chapter-60.md:249–255`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:887`). Seln: case shut, contents unnamed, undecided (`chapter-56.md:149`; `chapter-60.md:57–61`). Technician's sheet stays at the foot of the flat's second row, date unwritten (`STATE_LEDGER.md:900`).
+- Two unpaid non-money debts remain: Vastin for the eleventh and Teague for the thirteenth; neither man knows what Cael took (`chapter-60.md:25–33`; `BOOK_MAP.md:34`). Cael owes Lira the road-telling about the centre (`chapter-59.md:217–225`); Oryn is owed no leaf promise on this road because she explicitly defers it until she has to hear it (`chapter-60.md:197–203`).
+
+### Who knows what
+
+- Mechanism: the six including Oryn, not Vastin, Teague, Pike or Teague's crew (`AUTHOR-REPORT.md:164`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:896`).
+- Thirteenth: Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln and now Oryn; not Teague or Vastin (`chapter-56.md:275–295`; `chapter-57.md:53–59`; `BOOK_MAP.md:34`).
+- Eleventh: Cael/Lira/log readers as closed; not Vastin. Twelfth exists to the six and Cleon; the inward words/shape and matching court-floor read are Cael's alone (`chapter-57.md:179–241,261–297`; `chapter-59.md:49–77`). Lira knows only that a deliberate entry exists and remains unread (`chapter-57.md:261–297`).
+- Centre/no edge: Cael alone. Oryn has the same post-centre clinical finding as before; the rim group has only Cael's count and `nothing happened / nothing went` (`chapter-59.md:189–241`).
+- Court measures, copied slip, agreeing edges and no sixth: the rim group, including Vastin; Teague has the operational outline. Deep-layer date: Cael and Seln separately only. Two seals: Vastin only. Oryn has not heard the leaf. Teague's crew knows no mechanism, fragment, leaf, lamps page, slips, date or Vastin identity (`chapter-58.md:139–253`; `chapter-60.md:57–71`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:149,164`).
+
+### Deliberately open threads
+
+- The third sentence past *exclude* and *prevent*; Cael's identity; Book 9's word `recurrence` and the tomb remain entirely unspent (`chapter-59.md:179–185`; `chapter-60.md:277`; `BOOK_MAP.md:422,428,490`).
+- Vastin's formal request and the 3–2 vote remain for Book 9; Seln's deciding vote is untouched (`chapter-59.md:309–323`; `chapter-60.md:249–265`; `BOOK_MAP.md:424,490`).
+- The leaf and lamps finding remain separate; Vastin's apparatus sentence remains stopped; the directive/objection crack remains closed under unnamed seals (`chapter-59.md:323`; `BOOK_MAP.md:37–38,421,425`).
+- Instrument drift, dark Arbiter, running deep layer, chronicle hole, five-site bearing, missing first-tier example, Rune finding and the still place remain unresolved (`chapter-57.md:103–177`; `chapter-59.md:49–185`; `BOOK_MAP.md:34–38,421–431`).
+- Teague's grief and after-next-thaw return; Oryn's three holds and after-thaw map term; Cleon under Treswick; faceless faction; Seln's undecided case; Cael's two acquisition debts all remain live (`chapter-56.md:3–59`; `chapter-57.md:3–99`; `chapter-60.md:103–265`; `BOOK_MAP.md:40–45,490`).
