+# Verdict — REPAIR
+
+**Scope: bounded line repair, not a structural rewrite.** The movement is sound in sequence, calendar, causality, Reader Standard, deployment arithmetic and Book 9 handoff. It is not ratifiable while ten protected-text markers remain in the manuscript (`chapter-54.md:93`; `chapter-55.md:371`; `chapter-57.md:229`; `chapter-58.md:185,309,323,341,357`; `chapter-60.md:151,203`), one protected source tag is altered (`chapter-59.md:225`), a required day-count exchange is still a marker (`chapter-59.md:243`), Karis's exit injury omits the promised scar (`chapter-60.md:179`), Vastin receives a forbidden age anchor (`chapter-59.md:269`), one unprotected year span violates #58's limit (`chapter-60.md:17`), one sentence gives instruments intentional agency (`chapter-59.md:147`), one sentence falsely says Vastin has never asked anything of the group (`chapter-60.md:255`), and one sentence is grammatically broken (`chapter-59.md:73`). The exact repair is the eighteen fixes at the end of this audit.
+
+## 1. Continuity with the closed text
+
+### 1.1 Entry seam and carried state
+
+| Item | Ruling | Evidence |
+|---|---|---|
+| Place, time and company | **KEEP.** First light on the 306th, four or five miles short of the square notch, twelve people and the mule are carried cleanly from the closed shale camp. | `chapter-53.md:231–275`; `chapter-54.md:3–19`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:896–900`; `EVENT-LIST.md:7–12` |
+| Fragments and deployment at entry | **KEEP.** Thirteen fragments and deployment thirty-three are unchanged until Force is used. | `chapter-53.md:263–275`; `chapter-54.md:5`; `chapter-57.md:247–259`; `EVENT-LIST.md:7,35,52,62` |
+| Purse | **KEEP.** 123 is carried at every entry and no money is spent: 123 on the 306th, 307th night and movement close. | `chapter-47.md:227,299`; `chapter-48.md:99,321`; `chapter-57.md:247`; `chapter-58.md:221`; `chapter-60.md:9`; `EVENT-LIST.md:60` |
+| Vastin | **KEEP after fix 13.** He enters day twenty-seven, is twenty-eight on the 307th and twenty-nine on the 308th. The right knee remains on Oryn's linen/laths and the stick. The seated Wall does not spend the knee. The only contradiction is the new `since he was fourteen` age anchor. | `chapter-53.md:273`; `chapter-54.md:121,151–171`; `chapter-57.md:247`; `chapter-58.md:221`; `chapter-59.md:243,269`; `chapter-60.md:9,183–191`; `BOOK_MAP.md:39,44,438` |
