+# Verdict — REPAIR
+
+**Scope: bounded line repair, not a structural rewrite.** The movement is sound in sequence, calendar, causality, Reader Standard, deployment arithmetic and Book 9 handoff. It is not ratifiable while eleven protected-text markers remain in the manuscript (`chapter-54.md:93`; `chapter-55.md:371`; `chapter-57.md:229`; `chapter-58.md:185,309,323,341,357`; `chapter-59.md:243`; `chapter-60.md:151,203`), one protected source tag is altered (`chapter-59.md:225`), Karis's exit injury omits the promised scar (`chapter-60.md:179`), Vastin receives a forbidden age anchor (`chapter-59.md:269`), one unprotected year span violates #58's limit (`chapter-60.md:17`), one sentence gives instruments intentional agency (`chapter-59.md:147`), one sentence falsely says Vastin has never asked anything of the group (`chapter-60.md:255`), and one sentence is grammatically broken (`chapter-59.md:73`). The exact repair is the eighteen fixes at the end of this audit.
+
+## 1. Continuity with the closed text
+
+### 1.1 Entry seam and carried state
+
+| Item | Ruling | Evidence |
+|---|---|---|
+| Place, time and company | **KEEP.** First light on the 306th, four or five miles short of the square notch, twelve people and the mule are carried cleanly from the closed shale camp. | `chapter-53.md:231–275`; `chapter-54.md:3–19`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:896–900`; `EVENT-LIST.md:7–12` |
+| Fragments and deployment at entry | **KEEP.** Thirteen fragments and deployment thirty-three are unchanged until Force is used. | `chapter-53.md:263–275`; `chapter-54.md:5`; `chapter-57.md:247–259`; `EVENT-LIST.md:7,35,52,62` |
+| Purse | **KEEP.** 123 is carried at every entry and no money is spent: 123 on the 306th, 307th night and movement close. | `chapter-47.md:227,299`; `chapter-48.md:99,321`; `chapter-57.md:247`; `chapter-58.md:221`; `chapter-60.md:9`; `EVENT-LIST.md:60` |
+| Vastin | **KEEP after fix 13.** He enters day twenty-seven, is twenty-eight on the 307th and twenty-nine on the 308th. The right knee remains on Oryn's linen/laths and the stick. The seated Wall does not spend the knee. The only contradiction is the new `since he was fourteen` age anchor. | `chapter-53.md:273`; `chapter-54.md:121,151–171`; `chapter-57.md:247`; `chapter-58.md:221`; `chapter-59.md:243,269`; `chapter-60.md:9,183–191`; `BOOK_MAP.md:39,44,438` |
+| Oryn | **KEEP.** Six, seven and eight days past the cairn; she has not heard the leaf; the thirteenth is first told to her during the rib reading. | `chapter-54.md:299`; `chapter-56.md:253–305`; `chapter-57.md:43,91`; `chapter-58.md:221`; `chapter-60.md:9,177,197–203`; `BOOK_MAP.md:40,440` |
+| Teague and crew | **KEEP.** Teague's right arm remains on a slat and he takes the stair left-handed; the broad man's right shin is boarded, his right shoulder is newly bound; the tall man is unhurt; the unnamed young one dies; the lean old woman remains unnamed and does not speak to the six. | `chapter-54.md:247,315–329`; `chapter-55.md:97–147,257–293,323–327`; `chapter-60.md:125–165`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:883`; `EVENT-LIST.md:9` |
+| Six's bodies | **KEEP after fix 16.** Brom's left forearm is bound and his chest keeps its week of colours; Cael has two cracked ribs along the old line and a third sore rib; Karis's left palm remains bound, but the required scar promise is missing at `chapter-60.md:179`; Lira's arm remains whole. | `chapter-55.md:5–33`; `chapter-56.md:249–305`; `chapter-60.md:179,227–247`; `BOOK_MAP.md:44` |
+| Pages and objects | **KEEP.** Lamps leaf remains in Karis's notebook; fair leaf copy remains in Hesk's book; technician's sheet remains in the flat with its date unsaid; sealed slips remain unjoined; Hesk's dividers are used only by Karis; the tarred case contains cord, mallet and undriven stake thirty-two. | `chapter-57.md:103–165`; `chapter-58.md:189–203`; `chapter-60.md:247–253`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:900`; `EVENT-LIST.md:11` |
+| Knowledge at entry | **KEEP.** Oryn learns the thirteenth at the ribs. Teague and Vastin remain untold; Teague sees a moved heap and Cael's bill but is not told the mechanism, the fragment or its provenance. | `chapter-55.md:159–183,305–317`; `chapter-56.md:275–295`; `chapter-57.md:53–59,249–251`; `chapter-60.md:147–149`; `BOOK_MAP.md:34` |
+
+The exit sentence at `chapter-60.md:255` is nonetheless false as written: Vastin has asked Oryn to amend her term (`chapter-54.md:121–125`) and has asked the group many ordinary questions in closed text. The intended fact is narrower—he has not asked to be admitted (`BOOK_MAP.md:39,424`)—so fix 18 narrows it.
+
+### 1.2 The pass, the death and Force
+
+- **Seln's reconnaissance is sufficient.** The shelf, rig, nine-or-ten and three crossbows appear at `chapter-54.md:19–35`. The seven from the Span are among the larger pass team by the repeated cough at `chapter-56.md:71–83`; no plan text requires the pass team to consist only of the Span seven (`EVENT-LIST.md:18`).
+- **The wall is honest and compatible.** Vastin asks the person who owns the medical term, Oryn reads the knee after consent, and she amends only the manner of raising the Wall (`chapter-54.md:117–181`). The plane is still rooted through a ground contact, immobile while raised, and spends him to the stones (`chapter-54.md:337–361`; `chapter-55.md:333–347`). This does mint one bounded capability: an Iron Wall can be raised seated when the practitioner sets another part of the body upon the ground. Later books must honour that demonstrated case. It does not contradict the cut or alley, where the Wall was raised upright through the feet (`chapter-54.md:153–165`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:808,844`).
+- **Seven volleys and fixed casualties reconcile.** Brom is hit on one; the Wall rises on two; pine and first stack close the western mouth on four; the broad man is hit at the high edge on five; the young one goes one stride out and dies on six; Seln comes over the lip on seven (`chapter-54.md:321–353`; `chapter-55.md:3–147,191`).
+- **The death passes Reader Standard.** The hurt man's look, not an order, sends the boy; the tall man's hand misses; Lira is twenty strides away; `Leave me!` is the broad man's emergency shout, not a newly social speaking role (`chapter-55.md:97–121`). The wound is not described, the body “sat down,” and Oryn's failed attempt is brief (`chapter-55.md:113–139`). Teague's protected wall sentence sets cost rather than blame (`chapter-55.md:351–359`); Seln refuses exculpatory arithmetic (`chapter-56.md:127–139`); Karis gives Vastin presence, not absolution (`chapter-55.md:343–347`; `chapter-56.md:53–57`).
+- **Consent at an impossible moment is handled honestly.** Oryn asks, waits a breath, acts because the boy cannot answer, and later refuses to call that leave (`chapter-55.md:131–139`; `chapter-57.md:17–27`). This is the precise Reader Standard exception the event plan describes (`EVENT-LIST.md:32,42`).
+- **Force's first use is correct.** The brace, prop and second stack move east along the shelf into the hollow, not off the shelf and not at a person; Cael checks the line first; the recoil stops in the old ribs (`chapter-55.md:199–253`). Teague is on the stair with his face to the rock. Afterward he sees the heap and Cael holding his ribs and recognizes a paid bill (`chapter-55.md:305–311`). He therefore suspects that Cael paid for an unseen act; he does **not** know that a fragment came from him, that Force moved the heap, or whose capability it was. This satisfies “not told”; the stronger phrase “does not suspect” in Owner flag 6 overstates the governing plan (`STATE_LEDGER.md:883,896`).
+- **The retreat is clean.** Teague climbs left-handed; the tall man reverses **his** spear, carries the butt foremost, then grounds it as a taken touch; nine withdraw east; none is struck, taken or pursued (`chapter-55.md:257–299`).
+- **The win sentence stands.** `chapter-55.md:303` is the author's restatement of `BOOK_MAP.md:326` and `EVENT-LIST.md:37`. The Movement 9 win sentence is in §8, explicitly “private staging the author owns” (`BOOK_MAP.md:321`), and is absent from §10 (`BOOK_MAP.md:343–412`). It is **not protected**. Do not replace it with the plan's sentence.
+
