+# Verdict — REPAIR
+
+**Scope: bounded line repair, not a structural rewrite.** The movement is sound in sequence, calendar, causality, Reader Standard, deployment arithmetic and Book 9 handoff. It is not ratifiable while eleven protected-text markers remain in the manuscript (`chapter-54.md:93`; `chapter-55.md:371`; `chapter-57.md:229`; `chapter-58.md:185,309,323,341,357`; `chapter-59.md:243`; `chapter-60.md:151,203`), one protected source tag is altered (`chapter-59.md:225`), Karis's exit injury omits the promised scar (`chapter-60.md:179`), Vastin receives a forbidden age anchor (`chapter-59.md:269`), one unprotected year span violates #58's limit (`chapter-60.md:17`), one sentence gives instruments intentional agency (`chapter-59.md:147`), one sentence falsely says Vastin has never asked anything of the group (`chapter-60.md:255`), and one sentence is grammatically broken (`chapter-59.md:73`). The exact repair is the eighteen fixes at the end of this audit.
+
+## 1. Continuity with the closed text
+
+### 1.1 Entry seam and carried state
+
