+
+The S22 oath is continuous, not a contradiction. Oryn required the log promise not to approach the station steps or square at `chapter-19.md:95–109`, and the promise was kept through Treswick. The separate Book 7 self-reading exchange explicitly declined to demand a promise; the S22 wording says only “a healer made me swear an oath,” not that the oath concerned the Rune finding (`BOOK_MAP.md:396,409`).
+
+The S22 log does not tell Lira the finding on the page: she is handed the shut book, is asked not to read that leaf, and pushes it back unread (`chapter-57.md:261–297`). She learns that he deliberately took a costly look and wrote it, but not *Still / Set / Bones*, the shape, or the same-kind finding. Chapters 58–60 never rely on her having read it (`chapter-58.md:3–357`; `chapter-59.md:3–245`; `chapter-60.md:3–277`).
