+| Same-kind sentence | `Then he thought one thing, because it was the only thing that was a finding and not a guess, and he entered it exactly: the same kind of thing, to that instrument, as the sites were to Cleon's.` The following source paragraph adds the same-kind/not-same-thing limitation and Cleon's examples; none is part of the protected sentence (`source chapter-22.md:83–85`). |
